msgstr "If props placed with Anarchy have been accidently culled, you can press this button to bring them back now. This doesn't negatively effect performance."

#: Anarchy
msgid "Options.OPTION[Anarchy.Anarchy.AnarchyMod.AnarchyModSettings.AllowPlacingMultipleUniqueBuildings]"
msgstr "Allow Placing Multiple Unique Buildings"

#: Anarchy
msgid "Options.OPTION_DESCRIPTION[Anarchy.Anarchy.AnarchyMod.AnarchyModSettings.AllowPlacingMultipleUniqueBuildings]"
msgstr "This allows you to place multiple copies of unique buildings using the normal UI menu with or without Anarchy enabled. The effects of these buildings stack!"

#: Anarchy
msgid "Options.OPTION[Anarchy.Anarchy.AnarchyMod.AnarchyModSettings.MinimumClearanceBelowElevatedNetworks]"
msgstr "Minimum Clearance Below Elevated Networks"

#: Anarchy
msgid "Options.OPTION_DESCRIPTION[Anarchy.Anarchy.AnarchyMod.AnarchyModSettings.MinimumClearanceBelowElevatedNetworks]"
msgstr "With the net tool and Anarchy enabled you can violate the clearance of other networks. Zoning under low bridges can spawn buildings while doing this. This setting gives you some control over the minimum space below a low bridge. It would be better to just remove the zoning."

#: Anarchy
msgid "Options.OPTION[Anarchy.Anarchy.AnarchyMod.AnarchyModSettings.PreventOverrideInEditor]"
msgstr "Anarchy Components In Editor"

#: Anarchy
msgid "Options.OPTION_DESCRIPTION[Anarchy.Anarchy.AnarchyMod.AnarchyModSettings.PreventOverrideInEditor]"
msgstr "In the editor, with Anarchy and this option enabled, you can place vegetation and props overlapping or inside the boundaries of other objects and close together. The map may require Anarchy as a dependency. When users draw roads through these objects they will not be overriden. Also allows you to Lock Elevation in the editor."

#: Anarchy
msgid "Options.OPTION[Anarchy.Anarchy.AnarchyMod.AnarchyModSettings.DisableAnarchyWhileBrushing]"
msgstr "Disable Anarchy Toggle While Brushing Objects"

#: Anarchy
msgid "Options.OPTION_DESCRIPTION[Anarchy.Anarchy.AnarchyMod.AnarchyModSettings.DisableAnarchyWhileBrushing]"
msgstr "Automatically disables the anarchy toggle while brushing objects such as trees. Toggle reverts back to previous state after you stop brushing objects."

#: Anarchy
msgid "Options.OPTION[Anarchy.Anarchy.AnarchyMod.AnarchyModSettings.ShowElevationToolOption]"
msgstr "Show Elevation Option for Objects"

#: Anarchy
msgid "Options.OPTION_DESCRIPTION[Anarchy.Anarchy.AnarchyMod.AnarchyModSettings.ShowElevationToolOption]"
msgstr "Allows trees, plants, and props to be placed at different vertical elevations with Object Tool or Line Tool. Also shows a button during placement for locking elevation. Keybinds are configurable in the Keybinds tab."

#: Anarchy
msgid "Options.OPTION[Anarchy.Anarchy.AnarchyMod.AnarchyModSettings.ResetElevationWhenChangingPrefab]"
msgstr "Reset Elevation When Selecting New Asset"

#: Anarchy
msgid "Options.OPTION_DESCRIPTION[Anarchy.Anarchy.AnarchyMod.AnarchyModSettings.ResetElevationWhenChangingPrefab]"
msgstr "Automatically resets object Elevation tool option when you change to a new asset selection."

#: Anarchy
msgid "Options.OPTION[Anarchy.Anarchy.AnarchyMod.AnarchyModSettings.ResetNetworkToolOptionsWhenChangingPrefab]"
msgstr "Reset Network Tool Options When Selecting New Asset"

#: Anarchy
msgid "Options.OPTION_DESCRIPTION[Anarchy.Anarchy.AnarchyMod.AnarchyModSettings.ResetNetworkToolOptionsWhenChangingPrefab]"
msgstr "Automatically resets Network Anarchy and Network Upgrades tool options when you change to a new asset selection."

#: Anarchy
msgid "YY_ANARCHY.Anarchy"
msgstr "Anarchy"

#: Anarchy
msgid "YY_ANARCHY.AnarchyButton"
msgstr "Anarchy"

#: Anarchy
msgid "YY_ANARCHY_DESCRIPTION.AnarchyButton"
msgstr "Disables error checks for tools and does not display errors. When applicable, you can place vegetation and props (with DevUI 'Add Object' menu) overlapping or inside the boundaries of other objects and close together."

#: Anarchy
msgid "Anarchy.TOOLTIP_DESCRIPTION[PreventOverrideButton]"
msgstr "Allows placement of vegetation and props overlapping or inside the boundaries of other objects and close together."

#: Anarchy
msgid "Anarchy.TOOLTIP_TITLE[PreventOverrideButton]"
msgstr "Prevent Override"

#: Anarchy
msgid "Anarchy.TOOLTIP_TITLE[AnarchyModComponets]"
msgstr "Anarchy Mod Components"

#: Anarchy
msgid "Anarchy.TOOLTIP_DESCRIPTION[IncreaseElevation]"
msgstr "Increases the elevation relative to the placement surface. Customize keybind in options menu."

#: Anarchy
msgid "Anarchy.TOOLTIP_DESCRIPTION[DecreaseElevation]"
msgstr "Decreases the elevation relative to the placement surface. Customize keybind in options menu."

#: Anarchy
msgid "Anarchy.TOOLTIP_DESCRIPTION[ElevationStep]"
msgstr "Changes the rate in which the elevation changes. Customize keybind in options menu."

#: Anarchy
msgid "Anarchy.TOOLTIP_TITLE[ElevationLock]"
msgstr "Transform Lock"

#: Anarchy
msgid "Anarchy.TOOLTIP_DESCRIPTION[ElevationLock]"
msgstr "Prevents game systems from changing position (including elevation) and rotation. You can still change position and rotation with mods."

#: Anarchy
msgid "Anarchy.TOOLTIP_DESCRIPTION[ResetElevation]"
msgstr "Resets Elevation to 0. Customize keybind in options menu."

#: Anarchy
msgid "Options.OPTION[Anarchy.Anarchy.AnarchyMod.AnarchyModSettings.ToggleAnarchy]"
msgstr "Toggle Anarchy"

#: Anarchy
msgid "Options.OPTION_DESCRIPTION[Anarchy.Anarchy.AnarchyMod.AnarchyModSettings.ToggleAnarchy]"
msgstr "A keybind to switch the Anarchy toggle on or off."

#: Anarchy
msgid "Options.OPTION[Anarchy.Anarchy.AnarchyMod.AnarchyModSettings.ResetElevation]"
msgstr "Reset Elevation"

#: Anarchy
msgid "Options.OPTION_DESCRIPTION[Anarchy.Anarchy.AnarchyMod.AnarchyModSettings.ResetElevation]"
msgstr "A keybind to reset the elevation value during placement."

#: Anarchy
msgid "Options.OPTION[Anarchy.Anarchy.AnarchyMod.AnarchyModSettings.ElevationStep]"
msgstr "Change Elevation Step"

#: Anarchy
msgid "Options.OPTION_DESCRIPTION[Anarchy.Anarchy.AnarchyMod.AnarchyModSettings.ElevationStep]"
msgstr "A keybind to change the rate in which the elevation value changes."

#: Anarchy
msgid "Options.OPTION[Anarchy.Anarchy.AnarchyMod.AnarchyModSettings.UseElevationMimics]"
msgstr "Mimic Vanilla Increase and Decrease Elevation Keybinds"

#: Anarchy
msgid "Options.OPTION_DESCRIPTION[Anarchy.Anarchy.AnarchyMod.AnarchyModSettings.UseElevationMimics]"
msgstr "The keybinds for Increase and Decrease network elevations from the vanilla game will be used for increasing and decreasing object elevations."

#: Anarchy
msgid "Options.OPTION[Anarchy.Anarchy.AnarchyMod.AnarchyModSettings.IncreaseElevation]"
msgstr "Increase Elevation"

#: Anarchy
msgid "Options.OPTION_DESCRIPTION[Anarchy.Anarchy.AnarchyMod.AnarchyModSettings.IncreaseElevation]"
msgstr "A keybind to increase the elevation value of objects during placement."

#: Anarchy
msgid "Options.OPTION[Anarchy.Anarchy.AnarchyMod.AnarchyModSettings.DecreaseElevation]"
msgstr "Decrease Elevation"

#: Anarchy
msgid "Options.OPTION_DESCRIPTION[Anarchy.Anarchy.AnarchyMod.AnarchyModSettings.DecreaseElevation]"
msgstr "A keybind to decrease the elevation value of objects during placement."

#: Anarchy
msgid "Options.INPUT_MAP[Anarchy.Anarchy.AnarchyMod]"
msgstr "Anarchy"

#: Anarchy
msgid "Options.OPTION[Anarchy.Anarchy.AnarchyMod/ToggleAnarchy/binding]"
msgstr "Press key"

#: Anarchy
msgid "Options.OPTION[Anarchy.Anarchy.AnarchyMod/ResetElevation/binding]"
msgstr "Press key"

#: Anarchy
msgid "Options.OPTION[Anarchy.Anarchy.AnarchyMod/ElevationStep/binding]"
msgstr "Press key"

#: Anarchy
msgid "Options.OPTION[Anarchy.Anarchy.AnarchyMod/Elevation/positive]"
msgstr "Increase key"

#: Anarchy
msgid "Options.OPTION[Anarchy.Anarchy.AnarchyMod/Elevation/negative]"
msgstr "Decrease key"

#: Anarchy
msgid "Options.OPTION[Anarchy.Anarchy.AnarchyMod.AnarchyModSettings.Version]"
msgstr "Version"

#: Anarchy
msgid "Options.OPTION_DESCRIPTION[Anarchy.Anarchy.AnarchyMod.AnarchyModSettings.Version]"
msgstr "Version number for the Anarchy mod installed."

#: Anarchy
msgid "Options.OPTION[Anarchy.Anarchy.AnarchyMod.AnarchyModSettings.NetworkAnarchyToolOptions]"
msgstr "Network Anarchy Tool Options"

#: Anarchy
msgid "Options.OPTION_DESCRIPTION[Anarchy.Anarchy.AnarchyMod.AnarchyModSettings.NetworkAnarchyToolOptions]"
msgstr "With this option enabled and while drawing networks, options for ground, elevated, tunnel, and constant slope will appear when applicable in the tool options panel."

#: Anarchy
msgid "Options.OPTION[Anarchy.Anarchy.AnarchyMod.AnarchyModSettings.NetworkUpgradesToolOptions]"
msgstr "Network Upgrades Tool Options"

#: Anarchy
msgid "Options.OPTION_DESCRIPTION[Anarchy.Anarchy.AnarchyMod.AnarchyModSettings.NetworkUpgradesToolOptions]"
msgstr "With this option enabled and while drawing networks, options for various network upgrades will appear when applicable in the tool options panel. (i.e. street trees, retaining walls, quays, etc.)"

#: Anarchy
msgid "Options.OPTION[Anarchy.Anarchy.AnarchyMod.AnarchyModSettings.ElevationStepSlider]"
msgstr "Elevation Step Slider Tool Option"

#: Anarchy
msgid "Options.OPTION_DESCRIPTION[Anarchy.Anarchy.AnarchyMod.AnarchyModSettings.ElevationStepSlider]"
msgstr "Adds a slider for Elevation Step to tool options panel while drawing networks."

#: Anarchy
msgid "Options.OPTION[Anarchy.Anarchy.AnarchyMod.AnarchyModSettings.NetworkUpgradesPrefabs]"
msgstr "Network Upgrades Assets (Requires Restart)"

#: Anarchy
msgid "Options.OPTION_DESCRIPTION[Anarchy.Anarchy.AnarchyMod.AnarchyModSettings.NetworkUpgradesPrefabs]"
msgstr "Adds assets for Retaining Wall, Quay, Elevated, and Tunnel as road upgrades in the vanilla asset menu. These were originally part of Extended Road Upgrades by ST-Apps and have been incorporated into this mod with permission."

#: Anarchy
msgid "Options.OPTION[Anarchy.Anarchy.AnarchyMod.AnarchyModSettings.ReplaceUpgradesBehavior]"
msgstr "Replace Upgrades By Default"

#: Anarchy
msgid "Options.OPTION_DESCRIPTION[Anarchy.Anarchy.AnarchyMod.AnarchyModSettings.ReplaceUpgradesBehavior]"
msgstr "With this option enabled and while replacing networks, upgrades will by default be removed/added per tool options toggles. If disabled, they will be preserved is possible by default. You can change the behavior in-game by selecting the individual replace toggles for each row of options."

